# CMO FACTORY (issue #19777) -- holdout path is validator-role checkout only
# (builder role must never see the held-out acceptance answers it is graded
# against). A builder-role workflow step MUST run
# factory/gtm/builder_checkout.sh before checkout, which sparse-checkout-
# excludes every path carrying this attribute. See
# factory/gtm/test_holdout_negative.sh for the proof. This is narrower than
# the "protected paths" set in docs/gtm/META.md SS5 (MISSION.md, harness/gtm/,
# .factory/gtm/locks/) -- those are PR-write-rejected by gate.py but stay
# builder-readable, since a builder must be able to read the mission/journeys
# to comply with them. Only the holdout answer key is read-blocked outright.
.factory/gtm/holdout/** gtm-checkout=validator-only